  "body": "Stacked on #2126 (merge #2126 first)\n\n## What changed\n- Added `AxisLimits.parent`, `AxisLimits.chain_order`, `pivot`, `offset`, `zero_offset`, `rollover`, and `sign_convention` in `crates/post/src/machine/def.rs` and `crates/post/src/machine/trunnion.rs`, keeping `Machine.axes` sorted by controller coordinate while `Machine::rotary_axes()` returns rotaries in `kinematics.default.parts` parent-child order.\n- Updated `collect_axes` and `parse_mch_with` in `crates/post/src/machine/parse.rs` to parse optional unit-scaled `pivot`/`offset` lengths, degree `zero_offset`, boolean `rollover`, `controller.rtcp`, and `sign_convention` (`tool_rh` | `table_rh`) under the unstated-limit rule.\n- Wired `trunnion_refusals` into `crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs` so invalid vectors, mismatched types, disagreeing `sign_convention`, or rotary keys on linear parts fail by name in both `parse_mch` and `validate_text`.\n- Extracted rotary/RTCP mirroring into `crates/post/src/post/machine_rotary.rs` so `mirror()` and `script_props()` honor `controller.rtcp = false`, emit `signConvention` (default `tool_rh`), and pass the ordered rotary chain to post scripts.\n- Guarded `tilt(p)` in `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps` to refuse tilted moves on multi-rotary machines when controller RTCP is false even if rotary clamp codes exist, matching `fanuc.cps`.\n- Bumped `PROJECT_VERSION` from 65 to 66 in `crates/app/src/project/file.rs` after preserving the v64/v65 barriers from main and documented trunnion schema semantics in `crates/app/src/project/apply.rs` and `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`.\n- Recorded architectural choices in `docs/decisions/1962-trunnion-schema.md`.\n\n## Cause\nThe `.mch` schema, validator, and post mirror had no representation for trunnion pivot/offset geometry, zero offset, rollover, parent-child chain order independent of `ctrl_coord` sorting, explicit `tool_rh`/`table_rh` sign convention, or an explicit `controller.rtcp: false` override. Non-vertical rotary axes always inferred controller RTCP geometrically, risking `G43.4` emission on non-RTCP trunnion controls.\n\n## Break-through controls before and after\n\nThese captures use the real Heights parameter controls in the headless egui renderer.\nThe before captures use `holes_page.rs` from `2ab7ae424^`, before the Break-through rows.\nOnly ignored bindings for the new model fields were added to compile that page.\nThe after captures use the current page. Thread uses an internal thread in both captures.\n\n| Operation | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Drill | ![Before Drill](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0017bf3c0/2162/before-drill.png) | ![After Drill](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0017bf3c0/2162/after-drill.png) |\n| Bore | ![Before Bore](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0017bf3c0/2162/before-bore.png) | ![After Bore](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0017bf3c0/2162/after-bore.png) |\n| Thread (internal) | ![Before Thread (internal)](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0017bf3c0/2162/before-thread.png) | ![After Thread (internal)](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0017bf3c0/2162/after-thread.png) |\n\n## Tests\n- Pins (`crates/post/tests/trunnion_schema.rs`, 0/4 passed before fix, 4/4 passed after final edit): `explicit_non_rtcp_trunnion_does_not_promise_controller_compensation`, `rotary_chain_order_preserved_when_controller_coordinates_differ`, `trunnion_fields_parse_and_mirror_with_unit_scaling`, `invalid_trunnion_fields_refuse_by_name`.\n- Pins (`crates/app/tests/trunnion_schema.rs`, 0/2 passed before fix, 2/2 passed after final edit): `validator_accepts_ac_trunnion_and_refuses_bad_fields_by_name`, `project_roundtrips_non_rtcp_trunnion_and_protects_version`.\n- Targeted app suites (`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test index_swing --test index_swing_horizontal --test trunnion_schema`): 13 + 13 + 2 passed.\n- Mutation 1: removed `chain_order` sorting in `crates/post/src/machine/trunnion.rs` (`rotary_axes`): `rotary_chain_order_preserved_when_controller_coordinates_differ` and `trunnion_fields_parse_and_mirror_with_unit_scaling` failed; restored and all 4 passed.\n- Mutation 2: reverted `crates/post/src/post/machine.rs`: 3/4 tests in `post::trunnion_schema` failed; restored and passed.\n- Mutation 3: reverted `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: `explicit_non_rtcp_trunnion_does_not_promise_controller_compensation` failed; restored and passed.\n- Mutation 4: reverted `crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs`: `validator_accepts_ac_trunnion_and_refuses_bad_fields_by_name` failed; restored and passed.\n- Mutation 5: reverted `crates/app/src/project/file.rs` to `base-2126`: `project_roundtrips_non_rtcp_trunnion_and_protects_version` failed; restored and passed.\n- Clippy and gate: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed (0 warnings); `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed (`post`, `motion`, `app`, `ui`; 0 failed).\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone (`git diff --stat base-2126 -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n- Full non-quick `cargo xtask gate` outside `gate quick --base upstream/main`.\n- Downstream CAM-side IK solve and G43.4-less 5-axis posting (`#1965`, `#1968`).\n- Interactive UI layout checks.\n\n## Overlaps\n- Originally stacked on `#2126`; the merge refresh preserves main's v64/v65 barriers and advances `PROJECT_VERSION` from 65 to 66.\n- Touches the same files in different functions or `PROJECT_VERSION` bumps (whichever merges second refreshes) with open PRs `#2151`, `#2149`, `#2140`, `#2136`, `#2134`, `#2125`, `#2123`, `#2115`, `#2101`, `#2092`, `#2077`, `#2048`, `#2024`, `#1821`, `#1738`, `#1681`, and `#468`.\n\nChangelog: BREAKING: Project format advances from v65 to v66 to preserve AC trunnion fields and explicit non-RTCP capability; v65 and older readers refuse v66 files. Add optional AC trunnion kinematics fields, rotary chain order, explicit sign convention, and `controller.rtcp` flag to the `.mch` schema and post mirror.\n\nFixes #1962\n\n",
